Title: Add Go unit tests for insertClosedHeader and removeBlockedByLine
Created: 2026-05-05
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-05-05T08:34Z claude created

--- body ---
`tickets/tools/go/close.go` has three pure functions: `appendLogLine`
(tested in `close_test.go` after the raid), `insertClosedHeader` (lines
152-178), and `removeBlockedByLine` (lines 135-150). The latter two have
zero Go unit tests and are covered only by shell integration tests.

**`insertClosedHeader(content, reason string) string`** — inserts
`Closed: <reason>` into the preamble and a timestamped close entry before
`--- body ---`. It is the most complex of the three: it must handle trailing
blank lines before `--- log ---`, the presence/absence of existing `Closed:`
headers, and content with no body separator (error path).

**`removeBlockedByLine(content, id string) string`** — removes the
`Blocked-by: <id>` line from the preamble when the blocker is closed. Edge
cases: multiple `Blocked-by:` lines, `Blocked-by:` as the last preamble line,
ID that does not appear (no-op).

Add cases to `tickets/tools/go/close_test.go` covering:
- `insertClosedHeader`: basic insertion, blank-line handling around `--- log ---`,
  missing `--- body ---` fallback
- `removeBlockedByLine`: removes the correct line, leaves other `Blocked-by:`
  lines intact, no-op when ID absent
